Vulnerability Description Example Reentrancy Recursive external call before state update; classic DAO hack pattern The DAO hack (2016, $60M) Integer Overflow Unchecked arithmetic in Solidity \(&lt;\) 0.8 wraps silently BECToken batch overflow Access Control <code>onlyOwner</code> missing; <code>initialize()</code> callable by anyone Parity Multisig freeze Flash Loan Attacks Uncollateralised loan within one transaction exploits price oracle Multiple DeFi protocols Bridge Vulnerabilities Cross-chain bridges hold large locked assets; complex validator logic Ronin Bridge ($625M, 2022) Rug Pull Developers drain liquidity pool; <code>mint()</code> with no cap Numerous DeFi tokens <pre><code>// VULNERABLE: state update after external call
function withdraw(uint amount) external {
    require(balance[msg.sender] &gt;= amount);
    (bool success,) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(""); // external call
    require(success);
    balance[msg.sender] -= amount;  // state updated AFTER call: reentrancy!
}

// FIXED: Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern
function withdraw(uint amount) external {
    require(balance[msg.sender] &gt;= amount);  // Check
    balance[msg.sender] -= amount;            // Effect (state update first)
    (bool success,) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}("");  // Interaction
    require(success);
}
</code></pre>
